{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463582",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 108,
      "videoOrder": 92,
      "sourceHash": "c06e51e87948bc9faa337f0af9ad989b35d9a9ec786c7a97229a60cef4ee7ab6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.36,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "So that's it for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 6.43,
          "en": "Component Communication module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.43,
          "end": 8.62,
          "en": "Again, another big module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.62,
          "end": 11.21,
          "en": "with a lot of important concepts taught,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.21,
          "end": 14.38,
          "en": "but in the end, really just a couple of core concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.38,
          "end": 16.21,
          "en": "which you need to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.21,
          "end": 19.36,
          "en": "to let your components talk to each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.36,
          "end": 20.81,
          "en": "Now in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.81,
          "end": 24.24,
          "en": "components are used to build user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.24,
          "end": 25.57,
          "en": "by combining them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.57,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "The great thing about components is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 30.91,
          "en": "that you can encapsulate logic in a template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.91,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "and split your code into multiple smaller pieces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.84,
          "end": 37.39,
          "en": "and that you can also reuse components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.39,
          "end": 41.63,
          "en": "for example, components that encapsulate list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.63,
          "end": 46.37,
          "en": "Components then form parent-child relations automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.37,
          "end": 50.87,
          "en": "If you use component B in the template of component A",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.87,
          "end": 54.82,
          "en": "then component A is a parent of component B,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.82,
          "end": 57.03,
          "en": "which would be the child in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.03,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "And if you have a component C",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 61.2,
          "en": "in the template of component B,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.2,
          "end": 66.2,
          "en": "C is a child of B and also kind of a child to component A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.23,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "That is what I talked about throughout this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 71.35,
          "en": "and what you saw in action as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.35,
          "end": 72.56,
          "en": "And this matters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.56,
          "end": 76.28,
          "en": "because when we talk about component communication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.28,
          "end": 77.75,
          "en": "you need to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.75,
          "end": 82.75,
          "en": "that Vue uses unidirectional data flows for communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.15,
          "end": 83.983,
          "en": "So basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.983,
          "end": 87.57,
          "en": "that we have ways of passing data down to a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.57,
          "end": 92.12,
          "en": "or also up from a component using a different concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.12,
          "end": 94.64,
          "en": "Well, and these are the concepts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.64,
          "end": 97.75,
          "en": "For passing data down we have Props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.75,
          "end": 101.83,
          "en": "This allows us to pass data from a parent to a child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.83,
          "end": 103.93,
          "en": "So props are used for just that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.93,
          "end": 106.786,
          "en": "and we should define props in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.786,
          "end": 110.38,
          "en": "in that child component which will receive them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.38,
          "end": 113.02000000000001,
          "en": "You can either just specify an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.02000000000001,
          "end": 115.96000000000001,
          "en": "to let you know about the props you want to receive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.96000000000001,
          "end": 118.17,
          "en": "or you go into greater detail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.17,
          "end": 119.61,
          "en": "and you also let Vue know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.61,
          "end": 121.7,
          "en": "which type of data you're expecting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.7,
          "end": 124.48,
          "en": "whether a prop is required and all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.48,
          "end": 126.23,
          "en": "You saw that in great detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.23,
          "end": 127.963,
          "en": "throughout this module as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.47,
          "end": 131.95,
          "en": "If you need the other direction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.95,
          "end": 133.87,
          "en": "so from child to parent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.87,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "you need Custom Events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 139.07,
          "en": "A component can emit a custom event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.07,
          "end": 142.27,
          "en": "with help of the built-in dollar sign emit method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.27,
          "end": 145.56,
          "en": "to let a parent component know about something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 145.56,
          "end": 147.23,
          "en": "and to trigger code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.23,
          "end": 150.123,
          "en": "or trigger a method in the parent component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.4,
          "end": 153.8,
          "en": "Custom events also can carry data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 153.8,
          "end": 155.65,
          "en": "as you saw throughout this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.65,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "so that you for example, can forward data the user entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 161.57999999999998,
          "en": "into some input fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.57999999999998,
          "end": 164.18,
          "en": "the idea of something which was selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 164.18,
          "end": 168.1,
          "en": "or whichever data you need in your use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.1,
          "end": 171.91,
          "en": "So we have parent-child and child-parent communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 171.91,
          "end": 175.82,
          "en": "What we don't have here is neighbor communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.82,
          "end": 178.95,
          "en": "So if we have two sibling elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.95,
          "end": 182.05,
          "en": "And I talked about this throughout the module as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.05,
          "end": 186.43,
          "en": "If you have a scenario where two neighbor components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.43,
          "end": 188.11,
          "en": "need to exchange data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.11,
          "end": 188.96,
          "en": "you will, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 188.96,
          "end": 191.9,
          "en": "always use the common parent component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 191.9,
          "end": 194.01,
          "en": "of these two sibling components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 194.01,
          "end": 195.65,
          "en": "store the data in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.65,
          "end": 198.57999999999998,
          "en": "and then talk to that parent from each sibling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 198.57999999999998,
          "end": 200.15,
          "en": "and pass the data down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 200.15,
          "end": 203.11,
          "en": "to the respective sibling components that need the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 203.11,
          "end": 205.64,
          "en": "So you always have parent-child in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 205.64,
          "end": 209.183,
          "en": "You don't have sibling communication or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 211.07,
          "end": 212.91,
          "en": "Sometimes you have the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 212.91,
          "end": 216.21,
          "en": "that you have a lot of components in the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 218.37,
          "en": "through which you need to pass your data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 218.37,
          "end": 220.05,
          "en": "or your custom event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.05,
          "end": 223.26,
          "en": "And for that you got this Provide-Inject pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 223.26,
          "end": 226,
          "en": "which I showed you at the end of this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 226,
          "end": 229.89,
          "en": "If your data needs to travel through a lot of components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 229.89,
          "end": 233.01,
          "en": "which basically just pass that data through,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 233.01,
          "end": 235.53,
          "en": "with help of Props or Custom Events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 235.53,
          "end": 239,
          "en": "then you might want to consider Provide-Inject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 239,
          "end": 242.52,
          "en": "That allows you to provide data in a parent component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 242.52,
          "end": 245.81,
          "en": "and then inject it into any child component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 245.81,
          "end": 248.39,
          "en": "no matter how deeply nested it is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 248.39,
          "end": 249.996,
          "en": "without passing the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 249.996,
          "end": 252.59,
          "en": "through multiple levels of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 252.59,
          "end": 255.24,
          "en": "with Props or Custom Events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 255.24,
          "end": 256.51,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 256.51,
          "end": 259.06,
          "en": "don't use Provide-Inject to replace",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 259.06,
          "end": 261.51,
          "en": "all your Props or Custom Events with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 261.51,
          "end": 263.36,
          "en": "Instead, really only use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 263.36,
          "end": 268,
          "en": "if you need this long range communication, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 268,
          "end": 269.98,
          "en": "And that really is all you need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 269.98,
          "end": 272.94,
          "en": "about Component Communication at this point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 272.94,
          "end": 276.72,
          "en": "Make sure you understood the concepts taught in this module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 276.72,
          "end": 278.65999999999997,
          "en": "and with that let's advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 278.65999999999997,
          "end": 281.943,
          "en": "and let's dig deeper into Vue and into components.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
